             "role": "type.h2",
             "text": "What it sells"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "element",
           "id": "el-story-body",
           "kind": "text",
           "paragraphs": [
            {
             "role": "type.body",
             "text": "Calder makes control valves, actuators and process instruments for refining, chemicals and water utilities."
            },
            {
             "role": "type.body",
             "text": "Original equipment wins the installed base; the installed base then buys spares, service and retrofits at roughly twice the margin for the life of the plant."
            },
            {
             "role": "type.body",
             "text": "That second revenue stream is what a strategic buyer is paying for, and it is the part of the model that does not move with the capital cycle."
            },
            {
             "role": "type.body",
             "text": "The installed base is the moat: a valve replaced under contract is replaced with the same maker's part, and the switching cost is a plant shutdown rather than a purchase order."
            },
            {
             "role": "type.body",
             "text": "Two thirds of aftermarket revenue is booked under multi-year service agreements, which is why the segment's margin does not move with the capital cycle."
            }
           ]
          }
         ],
         "weight": 4.0
